{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe01\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Unmapped, inconsistent authorization logic makes the bypass scope uncertain while incident exposure is active.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Contain the endpoint, preserve evidence, reproduce the bypass, and identify affected roles, resources, and request paths.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Enumerate authorization helpers and call sites, compare the vulnerable path with trusted patterns, generate focused tests, and scan for equivalent bypass conditions.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose the smallest verified containment and patch that closes the exploit without broad untested authorization rewrites; escalate systemically only if repeated or structurally shared defects are evidenced.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Security owner approves severity, exposure scope, customer impact, disclosure obligations, and whether evidence warrants repository-wide remediation.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"Incident commander may halt normal releases, revoke access, or require systemic escalation.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record the exploit path, missed control, affected helper patterns, detection gap, and criteria used to scope systemic work.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe02\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Two days and sparse intermittent failures limit causal identification unless evidence is captured on the failing execution.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Instrument the test and dependent services to retain synchronized traces, timing, retries, environment state, and failure artifacts.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Cluster failures by signature, compare first-run and retry traces, vary scheduling and dependency conditions, and correlate with infrastructure events.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Classify product race, test race, or infrastructure noise by reproducibility, causal trace evidence, and controlled perturbation; prefer the least speculative explanation.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The engineer chooses the highest-information experiments and reports confidence, unresolved alternatives, and the operational risk of each classification.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The test owner may stop broad experimentation at the two-day boundary and quarantine or escalate the test based on evidence.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Store traces, experiment conditions, classification rationale, and a deterministic follow-up test or monitoring requirement.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe03\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Live consumers and external clients require compatibility across independently timed reads, writes, and deployment cycles.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Inventory every producer, consumer, query, contract, and external client behavior before selecting the migration sequence.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate schema and code dependency graphs, add dual-read/write compatibility tests, instrument field usage, and validate backfill checksums.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select an expand-migrate-contract sequence with dual compatibility, staged backfill, observed adoption, and rollback at each irreversible boundary.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The migration owner approves contract versions, deprecation dates, client communication, data-integrity thresholds, and cutover readiness.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The database or incident owner can pause writes, backfill, or deprecation when integrity, error, latency, or adoption gates fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain the dependency inventory, compatibility guarantees, observed consumer behavior, migration metrics, and rollback outcomes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe04\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Six changes jointly confound attribution while latency has materially regressed and blanket rollback is costly.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Freeze related changes and establish a comparable p99 baseline segmented by route, dependency, traffic shape, and release version.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Build a change-to-signal timeline, compare cohorts, trace slow requests, and use targeted feature flags or canaries to isolate contributors.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose the smallest reversible mitigation that restores the most latency with acceptable error and business impact; preserve urgent fixes unless evidence implicates them.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The service owner prioritizes customer impact, acceptable degradation, and which mitigation can safely trade functionality for latency.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The on-call incident commander may disable individual changes, cap traffic, or roll back a bounded subset.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Capture the attribution evidence, latency budget impact, effective mitigation, and release-process gaps that allowed compounded regression.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe05\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"The security patch conflicts with serialization compatibility across 18 services, creating both vulnerability and rollout risk.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Assess exploitability and exposure, pin the vulnerable surface, and construct a service-by-service serialization compatibility matrix.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Run differential serialization tests, generate mixed-version fixtures, map transitive dependency paths, and canary patched readers and writers.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select the fastest risk-reducing sequence that meets the security threshold while maintaining a tested wire contract, using compensating controls where patching must wait.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Security and platform owners jointly accept residual vulnerability, compatibility exceptions, rollout order, and emergency containment.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The security incident authority may block deployment, isolate services, or require emergency upgrade despite compatibility disruption.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record exploitability assessment, wire-format invariants, service compatibility results, compensating controls, and upgrade sequencing.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe06\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Silent loss is measurable but its location, mechanism, and ownership are unknown.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Assign temporary accountability, preserve source and output snapshots, and trace one complete record path with counts at every boundary.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Add durable identifiers, stage-level counters, dead-letter capture, sampling, and reconciliation checks; replay affected windows where possible.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose controls that make loss detectable and localizable before optimizing throughput; prioritize the narrowest repair supported by evidence.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The operations owner decides remediation scope, customer or downstream notification, acceptable residual loss, and permanent ownership.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The pipeline owner may pause or reroute processing when reconciliation fails or loss exceeds the agreed threshold.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain the ownership map, reconciliation design, loss mechanism, affected data window, and prevention thresholds.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"swe07\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Existing callers depend on ambiguous behavior, so correcting semantics can silently change production outcomes.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Inventory call patterns and defect cases, then specify the intended semantics and incompatibilities explicitly.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Add contract tests, usage telemetry, codemods, overload or adapter paths, and differential tests between legacy and clarified behavior.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose an additive or versioned API with explicit names and deprecation migration when caller intent cannot be inferred safely.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The SDK owner approves semantic definitions, compatibility promises, migration messaging, and exceptions for legacy callers.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The release owner may halt rollout when compatibility tests, telemetry, or critical-client validation fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Document the ambiguity, caller interpretations, defect patterns, compatibility strategy, and deprecation evidence.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n01\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Thirty mechanisms and overlapping papers create selection risk unless discriminating evidence is separated from repeated claims.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define the conductivity-loss outcome, causal variables, feasible interventions, and evidence-quality criteria before choosing experiments.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate papers and datasets, extract mechanism-to-observation claims, build an evidence matrix, and rank experiments by information gain and feasibility.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select three experiments that best distinguish competing mechanisms under available constraints, with at least one result capable of falsifying the leading explanation.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The scientific lead sets feasibility bounds, acceptable uncertainty, and the decision threshold for advancing or discarding mechanisms.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The lead may stop an experiment when controls fail, measurements cannot distinguish hypotheses, or safety and resource bounds are exceeded.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Preserve the evidence matrix, deduplication rules, preregistered predictions, null-result interpretation, and mechanism updates.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n02\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"The conjecture's graph-class definition may be wrong, making computational confirmation irrelevant.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Formalize the graph class and quantifiers, test the statement against boundary cases, and separate definition errors from conjecture failures.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate minimal counterexamples, verify the 120 examples independently, run exhaustive searches on small instances, and track assumptions.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose the weakest corrected statement supported by proofs or counterexamples, not the version with the most examples.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The mathematician decides which definitions and conjecture revisions preserve the intended problem.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The proof owner may stop computation once a decisive counterexample, definition defect, or proof path settles the current statement.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record formal definitions, counterexamples, verified computations, assumptions, and the exact conjecture revision.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n03\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Only two reversible tests are affordable and competitor response can contaminate long-term interpretation.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"State the free-tier hypothesis, target segment, success metric, guardrails, exposure window, and competitor-response observations.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Model unit economics and cannibalization ranges, randomize eligible exposure, measure retention and conversion, and monitor competitor changes.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select two tests with maximum decision information and reversibility, requiring both customer value and bounded economic harm to advance.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The founder chooses risk appetite, strategic guardrails, and the threshold for continuing despite competitor adaptation.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The business owner can terminate a test immediately for margin, support, abuse, or retention guardrail breaches.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain hypotheses, cohort definitions, competitor observations, economics, test results, and the advance/stop rationale.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n04\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Unknown validation, data, retention, appeal, and legal conditions make a definitive compliant notice unsafe.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Create a requirements register and block publication until system behavior, data flows, retention, jurisdiction, and review ownership are verified.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Inventory processing and model outputs, generate a data-flow and retention map, test validation controls, and draft conditional language with traceable sources.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Use only claims supported by verified controls and applicable review; mark unknowns as pending rather than implying compliance.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"Legal, privacy, HR, and system owners approve factual accuracy, jurisdictional applicability, applicant rights, and operational commitments.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The accountable compliance owner may stop drafting or deployment when evidence is missing or a required control fails.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Maintain the requirements register, evidence links, decision log, control owners, and unresolved questions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n05\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"One instructor cannot manually individualize practice and reliably assess 90 mixed-level engineers.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Baseline skill levels and job-relevant communication needs using a short common diagnostic and sampling plan.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate leveled practice, adaptive assignments, rubric-based feedback, item banks, and progress dashboards with human review sampling.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose activities that maximize transfer to technical work and assessment reliability within instructor review capacity.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The instructor sets proficiency standards, adjusts grouping, reviews borderline work, and decides advancement or remediation.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The instructor may stop an activity or assessment when validity, accessibility, workload, or learner-safety signals fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain diagnostic results, rubric revisions, item performance, intervention effects, and subgroup gaps.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n06\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Arrival and downtime variability are unknown, but urgent samples must remain protected without invented capacity.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Map current queues, urgency classes, processing times, downtime states, and real available capacity from observed records.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Simulate priority and reservation policies using bounded scenarios, instrument queue aging, and trigger downtime contingencies from actual state.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select a policy that protects urgent turnaround under tested worst-case scenarios while exposing assumptions and preserving manual override.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The lab manager sets clinical priorities, acceptable delays, staffing rules, and escalation thresholds.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The clinical operations authority may override or suspend the schedule when urgent risk, equipment failure, or unsafe workload occurs.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record observed distributions, policy assumptions, scenario results, queue outcomes, and overrides.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n07\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"A single wayfinding system must work across four languages, visual impairments, hospital stress, and changing routes.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define critical destinations, user journeys, accessibility requirements, language coverage, and environmental constraints with representative users.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate sign-system alternatives, test legibility and route comprehension, model decision points, and analyze error patterns by user group.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select the system with the lowest critical navigation error and strongest accessibility evidence, subject to maintainability and translation fidelity.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The hospital design and accessibility owners approve language, clinical terminology, cultural fit, and deployment priorities.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The facility authority may halt rollout when users cannot reach critical destinations reliably or accessibility requirements fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain test protocols, user-group results, translation decisions, error locations, and maintenance rules.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n08\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"A board decision needs compression without losing minority evidence or exposing participant identities.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Establish an anonymization protocol, coding frame, decision question, and explicit rule for preserving dissenting or low-frequency findings.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate transcripts, cluster themes, quantify prevalence with uncertainty, detect contradictions, and generate an evidence-to-decision trace.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select recommendations by decision relevance and evidence strength while reporting minority signals separately when their risk or strategic implication is material.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The research lead validates interpretations, protects confidentiality, and decides what uncertainty the board must see.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The privacy or research owner may block synthesis when re-identification risk or evidentiary distortion cannot be controlled.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain the coding schema, anonymization checks, dissent log, evidence trace, and decision outcomes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n09\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Fast field change and contaminated comparisons make apparent consensus unreliable.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define the field boundary and evidence schema, then build a provenance-first inventory of datasets, benchmarks, versions, and claims.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Deduplicate records, detect shared datasets and benchmark leakage, align evaluation protocols, and flag contradictory results by population and method.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Rank conclusions by provenance, independence, recency, methodological fit, and replication; preserve contradictions where conditions differ.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The research owner decides taxonomy, inclusion boundaries, acceptable evidence quality, and which unresolved conflicts matter strategically.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The owner may freeze the map when provenance is insufficient or benchmark contamination prevents defensible comparison.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Maintain dataset lineage, leakage findings, protocol differences, contradiction register, and map version history.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n10\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Authored payoff ranges express scenarios, not empirical probability distributions.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Separate model assumptions from observed evidence and define cooperation outcomes across the payoff uncertainty set.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Run sensitivity, interval, adversarial, and parameter-sweep analyses; identify regime boundaries and replicate simulation code.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Select conclusions that survive broad plausible assumptions, labeling scenario dependence instead of assigning unsupported probabilities.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The model owner chooses payoff ranges, update rules, robustness criteria, and the interpretation appropriate to the decision.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The owner may stop when behavior is non-identifiable across assumptions or implementation checks fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain code, parameter provenance, sensitivity maps, regime boundaries, and the distinction between empirical and authored inputs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n11\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"Water demand, rainfall, and routes are unstable during a 72-hour window, while allocation errors can become life-threatening.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Establish protected populations, current stocks, confirmed access points, urgency tiers, and update cadence using verified observations only.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Generate route and demand scenarios, optimize allocations with reserve buffers, and recalculate plans as forecasts and road states update.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Choose the plan that maximizes protected urgent coverage and robustness under forecast uncertainty, with explicit fallback routes and reserves.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The emergency coordinator sets priority rules, equity constraints, reserve levels, and acceptable service degradation.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The incident authority may reroute, reallocate, or suspend a plan when safety, access, contamination, or supply thresholds fail.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record assumptions, forecast versions, allocation decisions, route failures, unmet demand, and update triggers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n12\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"One expert-month must cover eight correlated bets without mistaking shared evidence for independent support.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Define each bet's decision, evidence dependency, reversibility, minimum test, and value of information.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Build an evidence-correlation graph, estimate effort and learning yield, and generate portfolio allocations across staged experiments.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Allocate to bets with high decision value, differentiated evidence, and reversible next steps, while reserving capacity for cross-bet dependencies.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The portfolio owner sets strategic priorities, risk tolerance, correlation assumptions, and the threshold for reallocating effort.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The owner may stop or reallocate a bet when its information yield, feasibility, or independence falls below the agreed gate.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Retain the dependency graph, allocation rationale, experiment results, correlation updates, and reallocation triggers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"n13\",\n    \"binding_constraint\": \"The issue is isolated and low-value, with no evidence that broader intervention would create leverage.\",\n    \"first_action\": \"Correct the typo and verify the rendered sentence in its local context.\",\n    \"machine_work\": \"Run a focused spelling or diff check limited to the affected sentence.\",\n    \"selector\": \"Stop after verified correction because recurrence evidence and leverage are absent.\",\n    \"human_object\": \"The requester confirms the intended spelling if the typo is ambiguous.\",\n    \"stop_authority\": \"The task owner may stop immediately after local verification.\",\n    \"durable_learning\": \"Record only the correction; do not create a systemic rule without recurrence evidence.\"\n  }\n]"}}
